<mjml>
  <mj-head>
    <mj-font name="Source Sans Pro" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css?family=Source+Sans+Pro:200,400,700&display=swap" />

    <!-- defines the style for different tags -->
    <mj-style inline="inline">
      a {
        color: #fbc926; /* Make links this color */
      }
      p {
        margin: 0.2em 0; /* Adjusts vertical spacing */
      }
      h2 {
        text-decoration: underline; /* Adds underline */ margin-bottom: 0.1em; /* Adjust margin below */ color: #ffffff
      }
    </mj-style>
  </mj-head>

  <!-- defines the color of the background that the column of content sits on top of -->
  <mj-body background-color="#222">
    <!-- add an empty section for padding at the top of the email -->
    <mj-section> </mj-section>

    <!--  defines the background color behind the text -->
    <mj-section padding="0" background-color="#000000">
      <mj-column>
        <!-- insert a banner image -->
        <mj-image padding="0" width="600px" src="https://static.presidentscup.us/2025.11.20.hero-banner.png" alt="2026 President's Cup Competition Banner. #PRESCUP" />

        <!-- defines the text style (font and color) -->
        <mj-text font-family="Source Sans Pro, sans-serif" padding-top="20px" font-size="16px" color="#ffffff" line-height="1.3">
          <!-- insert email content here -->
          <p>
            <span><b>President's Cup 7 registration is now open until January 13 for Individuals and January 27 for Teams.</b></span>
          </p>
          <br />

          <p>
            <span>This year's competition is packed with exciting new challenges that will transport you in a spy-themed world! Get ready to go undercover and showcase your cyber skills against as you compete against the top cybersecurity talent in the federal government! Visit <a href="https://cisa.gov/presidentscup">cisa.gov/presidentscup</a> for more information and register today.</span>
          </p>
          <br />

          <h2>Key Dates to Remember:</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Registration closes for Individuals on January 13.</li>
            <li>Registration closes for Teams on January 27.</li>
          </ul>
          <br />

          <h2>What's New This Year?</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>The Individuals competition now takes place <b>before</b> the Teams competition.</li>
            <li>Tracks A &amp; B have been rebranded as "Defensive Track" and "Offensive Track," respectively.</li>
            <li>
              We're using a new competition platform designed to provide a streamlined experience. Please note that all participants must create a new login to compete.
              <a href="https://presidentscup.cisa.gov/pc7">Additional details can be found here</a>.
            </li>
          </ul>
          <br />

          <h2>Competition Details:</h2>
          <p>During the qualifying rounds, Individuals will have 4 hours per track to complete as many challenges as they can, and Teams will have 6 hours.</p>
          <br />

          <h2>President's Cup 7 Timeline</h2>
        </mj-text>

        <mj-image padding="0" width="600px" src="https://static.presidentscup.us/2025.11.20.timeline.png" alt="2026 President's Cup Competition Banner. #PRESCUP" />

        <mj-text font-family="Source Sans Pro, sans-serif" padding-top="20px" font-size="16px" color="#ffffff" line-height="1.3">
          <br />
          <p>We look forward to seeing you back in action for another exciting year of competition! If you have any questions, feel free to reach out to us at <a href="mailto:presidentscup@cisa.dhs.gov">presidentscup@cisa.dhs.gov</a>.</p>
          <br />
        </mj-text>

        <!-- show a button for the prescup site -->
        <mj-button padding-bottom="40px" font-family="Source Sans Pro, sans-serif" href="https://cisa.gov/presidentscup" background-color="#ff0a44" color="#ffffff" font-size="18px"> cisa.gov/<strong>presidentscup</strong> </mj-button>
      </mj-column>
    </mj-section>

    <!-- add an empty section for padding at the bottom of the email -->
    <mj-section> </mj-section>
  </mj-body>
</mjml>
